 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance authorizing The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County to abandon public sanitary sewer main and easements, and to accept new sanitary sewer main, sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at 1713 Primrose Avenue (MWS Project No. 25-SL-196 and Proposal No. 2026M-092ES-001).\n..body\nWHEREAS, the abandonment of approximately 94 linear feet of existing eight-inch sanitary sewer main (Lined VCP) and easements, and the acceptance of approximately 36 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 96 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), four sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at 1713 Primrose Avenue, are needed to construct Project No. 25-SL-196; and,\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Planning Commission approved mandatory referral No. 2026M092ES-001 on September 14, 2026, for the abandonment and acceptance of said sanitary sewer mains, sanitary sewer manholes and easements. \nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThe Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County is authorized to abandon approximately 94 linear feet of existing eight-inch sanitary sewer main (Lined VCP) and easements, and to accept approximately 36 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 96 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), four sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at 1713 Primrose Avenue, as shown on Exhibit 1, which are attached hereto and incorporated by reference:\nMap & Parcel: \t\t\t\tAddress:\n11708002500\t\t\t\t\t1713 Primrose Avenue\nSection 2.\tThe Directors of Water and Sewerage Services and Public Property Administration are authorized to execute such documents as may be necessary and appropriate to carry out the abandonment and acceptance authorized by this ordinance. \nSection 3.\tAmendments to this legislation shall be approved by resolution.\nSection 4.\tThis ordinance shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it. \n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis ordinance abandons approximately 94 linear feet of existing eight-inch sanitary sewer main (Lined VCP) and easements, and accepts approximately 36 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 96 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), four sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at 1713 Primrose Avenue.\n\nThis ordinance has been approved by the Planning Commission. Future amendments to this ordinance may be approved by resolution.\n\nFiscal Note: This ordinance has no cost to Metro. Donated and abandoned easements have no market value according to the Department of Water Services.\n\n"
